# THE-219 Part B independent source verdict

**Source approval, pending actual compilation and execution.** Reviewed the three files in `/tmp/thegn-maintenance-04-drain-20260914` against `/tmp/thegn-THE219-part-b-source-20260914.json`; all SHA256 hashes match. No Cargo, Git fixture, CLI, provider or benchmark execution by this reviewer.

The two Linux tests invoke the actual normal CLI for enqueue/list and two plain drains each. The private config is validated through both strict raw validation and concrete typed assertions. Environment clearing, null stdin, private state/config/cache/runtime/temp, only lexical Git/sh entrypoints on PATH, empty private Git config/hooks and disabled automation/sandbox/devshell/warmup prevent the proposed fixture from depending on user credentials or backend availability. The real agent resolves positively to an owned sentinel; the asserted infrastructure hold and missing sentinel establish that it was never launched. `route_to_host` cannot acquire an endpoint from the cleared environment; source `cmd/merge.rs` retains the local branch when no endpoint/remote marker is present.

The oldest-first timestamps and exact four-row ordered EVERY-status-UPDATE audit make continuation meaningful: held must fold and block once before clean folds and becomes ready. A second same-value folding update is also recorded, so the audit cannot hide repeated loops. The finite inherited attempt count remains one. First- and second-drain refs/worktree registrations/flat committed file bytes are compared, with autoland/removal disabled. The intentional repair phase allows only the exact held branch/HEAD and two declared file changes and requires unchanged queue rows. The second plain drain proves re-enumeration and readiness of that same row without spending attempts; it does not prove recovery of the sandbox floor (Part A addresses that separately). THE-608 is not claimed.

Custody retains a fixed slot before spawn and installs the returned Child immediately. It checks the non-auto-reaping disposition without changing it, observes the exact child with WNOWAIT, latches any observation/consuming-wait failure, signals the original group and owned child before consuming the one ready wait, and never resumes process syscalls after lost identity or reap. Deadlines and monitored regular-file capture are bounded; observation uncertainty/failure retains Child/root instead of discarding ownership. The requested statement-local blocking-wait lint expectation is present and justified by the already-ready private child. Success receipts require reaped leaders, no retained/error custody, and strict TempDir close before exporting evidence. This is owned fixture-group cleanup, not escaped-tree or native Windows/macOS containment.

No remaining scoped source revision requested. Native parser/config/DB/tool behavior and strict lint remain root gates; a successful source review cannot substitute for them. The 2MiB capture ceiling is monitored rather than an OS file quota, and branch snapshots do not claim byte-for-byte Git index preservation. These limits are stated rather than enlarged into unrelated fixture requirements.
